WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
On the eighth day after
a Jewish boy is born,

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.960
family and friends gather.

3
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.350
An empty, decorated chair
is set out for Elijah,

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.390
believed to be present
at every such ceremony.

5
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.060
Thirteen years later, the same boy may
stand at the bimah and read from a Torah

6
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:17.120
scroll.

7
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:22.150
So what do these ceremonies, at
birth and at 13, actually change?

8
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.730
In this mission, you'll trace these rites
back to God's covenant with Abraham.

9
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.050
Then you'll compare how Orthodox and
Reform communities mark a girl coming of

10
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.050
age.

11
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.410
Your mission: find out what the ceremonies
at birth and at 13 really change.
